{"availability":"available","full":"nina-mir/nina-mir","name":"nina-mir","description":"about me","category":"Other","language":null,"stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2023-09-06T18:51:10Z","updated":"2026-10-08T21:52:46Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://nina-mir.github.io/snarp-analysis/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T00:54:15.351Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T00:54:15.351Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T00:54:15.351Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T02:35:54.402Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T09:03:20.048Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T00:54:15.351Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["| browser-use/browser-use #5672 | Stopped two LLM provider adapters from authenticating third-party endpoints with the user's OpenAI key. ChatDeepSeek and ChatCerebras passed apikey=None into an AsyncOpenAI client pointed at api.deepseek.com and api.cerebras.ai, so the SDK fell back to OPENAIAPIKEY — sending it to a different vendor. The env vars the docs promised were never read. Audited all nine adapters to derive the discriminator (an OpenAI-SDK client at a non-OpenAI baseurl), which found exactly these two and cleared the rest; reported the negative results alongside the fix.","| | docling-project/docling #4457 | Found and fixed a bug nobody had reported: numbering inside a Word text box leaked onto the paragraph holding it. A floating text box is stored inside an anchor paragraph, but docling resolved list numbering with a descendant search (.//w:numPr) that reached into the box — so plain body text came out as a list item (issue #4456, which I filed). OOXML permits w:numPr only under w:pPr, so the search could only ever find another paragraph's numbering. Proved causality by diffing a full conversion with the lookup narrowed: exactly one line of the document…","| | python-visualization/folium 3 PRs | #2263 · Root-caused a bug open since 2021: GeoJSON tooltips came up empty on multi-geometry features. The feature never reached the child layers Leaflet wraps in a FeatureGroup (issue #1520). Fix verified against all eight geometry types plus nested GeometryCollections, with a Selenium regression test."],"features":["Filed adobe/react-spectrum #10411 with a live reproduction — the S2 docs playground was emitting Tooltip code samples that didn't typecheck; a maintainer shipped the fix the next day.","Posted browser-tested findings on react-spectrum #8027 and mdn/content #45005, including the negative results."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nina-mir/nina-mir/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f70d88ef5f04709eb973fddc6e75fec921b567d735baff1ec4116373226fef8d","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T11:47:25.607Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T11:47:25.607Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"| browser-use/browser-use #5672 | Stopped two LLM provider adapters from authenticating third-party endpoints with the user's OpenAI key. ChatDeepSeek and ChatCerebras passed apikey=None into an AsyncOpenAI client pointed at api.deepseek.com and api.cerebras.ai, so the SDK fell back to OPENAIAPIKEY — sending it to a different vendor. The env vars the docs promised were never read. Audited all nine adapters to derive the discriminator (an OpenAI-SDK client at a non-OpenAI baseurl), which found exactly these two and cleared the rest; reported the negative results alongside the fix.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nina-mir/nina-mir/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f70d88ef5f04709eb973fddc6e75fec921b567d735baff1ec4116373226fef8d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nina-mir/nina-mir/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T11:47:25.608Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T21:52:46Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nina-mir/nina-mir/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T11:47:25.609Z","hash":"f70d88ef5f04709eb973fddc6e75fec921b567d73